<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Petronilla of Aragon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1136–1173</span> · Also known as Petronila of Aragon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Petronilla was queen of Aragon from 1137 to 1164, the daughter and heiress of Ramiro II. Betrothed as an infant in 1137 to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramon-berenguer-iv-count-of-barcelona">Ramon Berenguer IV, Count of Barcelona</a>, who then governed Aragon, she married him in 1150. The union joined Aragon and the County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> in what became the Crown of Aragon, and in 1164 she abdicated in favour of their son Alfonso II.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/petronilla-of-aragon.jpg" alt="Petronilla of Aragon" width="320" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: derivative work: Escarlati (talk) Genealogía_Casa_de_Aragón.jpg: Genealogía anónima por iniciativa de Martín I de Ara... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peronella_reina.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
